# SPEC GOLDEN — hand-written from css-flexbox-1 §9.7 before the code did this,
# never regenerated.
#
# A replaced element is a flex item like any other: §9.7 resolves a main size
# for it, and that flexed size *is* its used main size. Its intrinsic width
# only reaches the algorithm twice — as the flex base size when `flex-basis`
# is `auto`, and as §4.5's content size suggestion — and neither of those is
# the used size. So an `<img>` under `flex: 1` stretches, exactly as a `<div>`
# does.
#
# `width="80"` is 80px = 10 cells (PLAN.md's 8px per cell), `height="16"` is
# 16px = 1 line.
#
# §9.2: `flex: 1` is `1 1 0`, so both items have a flex base size of 0. Their
#   hypothetical main sizes are that clamped by §4.5's automatic minimum: the
#   image's content size suggestion is its intrinsic 10 cells, the div's is
#   min-content = 1 cell.
# §9.7 step 1: sum of hypothetical outer main sizes = 10 + 1 = 11 < 80, so
#   this is a grow pass.
# §9.7 step 2: neither item is frozen — both grow factors are 1, and each
#   base size (0) is under its hypothetical main size.
# §9.7 step 4: free space = 80 - 0 - 0 = 80, split by grow factor 1:1, so each
#   item's target is 0 + 40 = 40. Neither violates its minimum (40 >= 10 and
#   40 >= 1), so both freeze and the loop ends.
#
# Whole cells: both targets are integral, so nothing is left over.
#
# The line is therefore filled exactly — 40 + 40 = 80 — which is the property
# that matters beyond this fixture. An image that kept its intrinsic 10 cells
# and advanced the cursor by 10 would leave the row holding 30 cells of free
# space that §9.7 had already given away, and M9.7's `justify-content` would
# then distribute a free space of zero across a row that visibly has room.
#
# The image's height is untouched: stretching on the main axis is what §9.7
# resolved, and the cross axis is M9.8's.
<html>  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=1
  <body>  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=1
    <div.row> flex row  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=1
      img "logo" https://fixture.test/logo.png  x=0 y=0 w=40 h=1
      <div.item>  x=40 y=0 w=40 h=1
        anonymous  x=40 y=0 w=40 h=1
          line  x=40 y=0 w=40 h=1
            #text "b"  x=40 y=0 w=1 h=1
